- If the tree is empty, return 0.
- If there is no left child, check only the right subtree.
- If there is no right child, check only the left subtree.
- If both children exist, choose the smaller depth.
You cannot simply use `Math.min()` for the two subtrees, because a missing child would return 0, leading to an incorrect result.

Time Complexity: O(n)

In the worst case, the algorithm visits each node in the tree once, so the number of operations is proportional to the number of nodes.

Space Complexity: O(h) — the recursion stack depends on the height of the tree.
 You can use BFS (Breadth-First Search). It traverses the tree level by level and stops as soon as the first leaf node is encountered.
